A freedive and spearfishing session at the Spit with the boys, working the boulders along the Seaway wall. Visibility was patchy: a bit green and stirred up in close, cleaner out over the sand, with enough swell running to make the entry interesting. A green turtle came past, sea mullet stacked up along the wall in their thousands, and a school of cownose rays crossed the sand flats on the way in. All three are tagged on screen as they appear, and there was a feed to take home at the end.

## Dive stats

- **Location:** Gold Coast Seaway (The Spit), QLD
- **Date:** 3 July 2026
- **Depth:** Avg 3m, Max 7m
- **Visibility:** 5-8m

## Highlights

Green Turtle, Sea Mullet, and Cownose Rays
